 after all he was teased in  spider-man homecoming  when his uncle aaron davis aka the  prowler mentioned that he had a nephew  the other night you told that dude if  you're gonna shoot somebody shoot me  it's pretty ballsy i don't want those  weapons in this neighborhood i got a  nephew who live here  this setup in spider-man homecoming  means that miles morales already exist  within the mcu and we were wondering  when that was going to come full circle  when they were going to  actually introduce him as a character  and apparently miles's future is big  and marvel has some big plans for him to  join the young avengers in the near  future with some other new  young heroes as well however adding  miles morales doesn't mean that tom  holland  is going anywhere despite him saying  that he's taken a break  after spider-man no way home but in fact  according to this report  marvel and sony still have big plans for  him and they plan to use him in a way  that we've never seen him before and  that is to see  spider-man in college but don't worry  i'll break down everything you need to  know about this new report in this video  and if you're new be sure to subscribe  so you don't miss out on any of the  latest  spider-man no way home news so this  report that spider-man is going to be  split into two different franchises  peter parker and miles morales is coming  from  that show.com and they start this  article off by mentioning a very good  point stating that it's an interesting  predicament that marvel and sony find  themselves in  spider-man homecoming made over 880  million dollars and spider-man far from  home  made over 1 billion the first spider-man  film to ever do so  and it's safe to assume that a movie  also starring tobey maguire and andrew  garfield could easily crack  at least 1.5 billion which is a cash cow  that marvel and sony aren't going to  want to walk away from  however you have the current actor tom  holland who is kind of aging out of the  role  almost being 25 in real life and you  also have director john watts who is  being shifted over to direct the  fantastic four  and according to kevin feige on the  investor day presentation they have  already begun to start working on the  fantastic four this means scripting and  filming will happen  relatively soon which means that john  watts is going to be tied up for let's  say  two to four years and perhaps maybe even  longer than that  so according to that hashtag show.com  when sony and marvel  disney entered those renegotiations a  while back that scared us all  having us thinking that spider-man might  not actually be a part of the mcu  anymore  apparently in these negotiations they  wanted to future proof  spider-man which is part of the reason  that they are going to do the  spider-verse  but according to that hashtag show.com  they have exclusively learned that sony  will continue making their  sp umc films or the sony pictures  universe of  marvel characters with marvel continuing  with spider-man as well  that means splitting the franchise in  two and this is what the hashtag show  says that they've heard about it they're  going to create two different franchises  one's going to be peter parker's story  and explore a storyline with him in  college or university  the other franchise is going to focus on  miles morales and it's said that marvel  is keen to use miles on their upcoming  young avengers project and they see a  lot of value in him which of course  who wouldn't he's an awesome character  and a fan favorite and there's a lot of  hype around the young avengers right now  especially if you consider that we just  got billy and tommy or  wiccan and speed in one division not to  mention kate bishop coming to the mcu  along with miss marvel and  other young heroes as well so it's all  kind of coming together here and miles  is a younger spider-man  and this does seem like kind of a  perfect opportunity to bring him in and  possibly have peter parker mentor him  which would also be really good because  a lot of people are kind of tired of  our peter parker having a mentor or a  coach  they want to see him kind of go at it on  his own so it would be really good if he  actually was the mentor himself but  continuing with that  show's report they say that from what  they've heard no way home is going to  provide us a much  clearer road map for spider-man in the  mcu  they want writers and directors who can  bring a distinct voice to each character  and the reason for this according to  this report is because marvel and sony  are concerned about  branding they're worried that having two  spider-man franchises at the same time  will confuse some general audience  members and having a strong vision  behind  each character is their primary strategy  now they do go on to say that there are  vague ideas of how to bring these two  characters together  for some sort of spider-man crossover  but that's years down the line  right now the focus is just on  introducing miles morales to the mcu  which again he kind of already was  because we met his uncle who mentioned  his nephew him  miles confirming that he does already  exist in the mcu  the focus now is going to be on his  introduction and it looks like that is  going to take place at some point  in some way during spider-man no way  home which makes sense now like i  mentioned in the beginning tom holland  said that he's going to be  taking a break now this does not mean  that he is done playing spider-man he  already said if they want him back he is  100 going to be there and as we know  of course they want him back a lot of  people really really love tom holland as  spider-man and there's no doubt that  he's been super super successful with  the character so he's definitely coming  back even though it is quite interesting  that john watts is now going to direct  the fantastic four  and in spider-man homecoming we had some  pretty big easter eggs for the fantastic  four  one